The function is already tiny, so the only change is a cheaper control flow. The common case (a valid profile and index) gets a branch hint and is handled first. The original's return values are unchanged, including `FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID` for a null profile or out-of-range index.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p != NULL, 1))
    {
        const FIT_UINT16 idx = profileIndex;
        if (__builtin_expect(idx < p->numFields, 1))
            return p->fields[idx].num;
    }
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```